    <string name="grayscale_toggles_hint" translatable="false">Color always comes back when you turn these off. You can also switch it back yourself in Settings > Accessibility > Color correction.</string>
    <string name="grayscale_grant_title" translatable="false">Allow grayscale</string>
    <string name="grayscale_grant_body" translatable="false">Android lets an app switch the screen to grayscale only after a one-time permission given through developer tools. Parem uses it for grayscale and nothing else.\n\nTo get color back at any time, without Parem: Settings > Accessibility > Color correction.</string>
    <string name="grayscale_grant_wifi" translatable="false">On this phone, over Wi-Fi:\n1. Turn on Developer options: Settings > About phone > tap Build number 7 times.\n2. In Developer options, turn on Wireless debugging and tap Pair device with pairing code.\n3. Pull down Parem\'s notification and type the 6-digit code into it.</string>
    <string name="grayscale_pair_start" translatable="false">Start pairing</string>
    <string name="grayscale_grant_computer" translatable="false">Or with a computer: turn on USB debugging, plug the phone in, and open this page in Chrome or Edge:</string>
